.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt NQTSPUT 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqtsreq ,
.Nm nqtsput
.Nd add an RFC 3161 timestamp to a sealed capsule
.Sh LIBRARY
libnoqtis, \-lnoqtis
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In noqtis.h
.Ft int
.Fo nqtsreq
.Fa "const char *dir"
.Fa "const uint8_t *nonce" "size_t noncelen"
.Fa "uint8_t *req" "size_t reqlen" "size_t *outlen"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo nqtsput
.Fa "const char *dir"
.Fa "const uint8_t *rsp" "size_t rsplen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *nonce" "size_t noncelen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *const *anc" "const size_t *anclen" "size_t nanc"
.Fa "int64_t *gt" "const char **why"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A timestamp from a time-stamping authority (TSA) shows that a seal's
signature existed at the time the TSA states.
The library makes no network request: the caller sends the request and
passes back the reply, as
.Xr noqtis-seal 1
.Fl -tsa
does over HTTP.
.Pp
.Fn nqtsreq
writes to
.Fa req
(of
.Fa reqlen
bytes) the DER RFC 3161
.Vt TimeStampReq
for the seal in the folder
.Fa dir :
version 1, the SHA-256 message imprint of the decoded
.Ql signature
of its
.Pa noqtis.sig ,
the
.Fa nonce
when it is not
.Dv NULL
(at most 32 bytes, big-endian; a leading zero is dropped and a sign byte
added as DER needs), and certReq TRUE, so that the TSA includes its
certificate.
The request is at most 128 bytes;
.Pf * Fa outlen
gets its size.
Send it with the media type
.Ql application/timestamp-query
(RFC 3161 section 3.4) and keep the nonce for
.Fn nqtsput .
.Pp
.Fn nqtsput
reads
.Fa rsp ,
the TSA's reply of
.Fa rsplen
bytes (a
.Vt TimeStampResp ,
or a bare token), and, when it checks, stores the token as the
.Ql timestamp
of
.Fa dir Ns 's
.Pa noqtis.sig ,
replacing any timestamp it has; every other field keeps its bytes.
It checks, in order, that:
.Bl -enum -compact
.It
.Pa noqtis.sig
is a canonical
.Ql noqtis-seal-1
seal;
.It
the reply is a strict DER RFC 3161 reply and its status is granted;
.It
the token's imprint is its hash (SHA-256, SHA-384 or SHA-512) of the
seal's signature;
.It
its nonce is
.Fa nonce ,
when that is not
.Dv NULL ;
.It
its CMS signature verifies under its signer certificate, which is a TSA
certificate (extendedKeyUsage critical and only timeStamping) valid at
genTime;
.It
with
.Fa nanc
anchors (DER X.509 certificates
.Fa anc Ns Bq i
of
.Fa anclen Ns Bq i
bytes, at most 32), that certificate's path leads to one of them and is
valid at genTime, as
.Xr nqchkt 3
checks it.
.El
Without anchors the reply is checked but the TSA is not trusted:
whether to trust it is decided when the capsule is checked, with
.Xr nqchkt 3 .
.Pp
.Pf * Fa gt ,
when
.Fa gt
is not
.Dv NULL ,
gets the token's genTime in seconds since the epoch;
.Pf * Fa why ,
when
.Fa why
is not
.Dv NULL ,
gets a sentence saying which check failed, or
.Dv NULL
on success.
Nothing is written unless every check passes.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Dv NQOK
(0), or a negative error code:
.Bl -tag -width NQEVRFY
.It Bq Er NQEARG
.Fa dir ,
.Fa req ,
.Fa outlen
or
.Fa rsp
is
.Dv NULL ,
.Fa rsplen
is 0, a nonce is over 32 bytes or
.Dv NULL
with a length, an anchor is
.Dv NULL
or empty, or an anchor is not a certificate.
.It Bq Er NQEBUF
.Fa reqlen
is too small.
.It Bq Er NQEDEC
.Pa noqtis.sig
is not a canonical
.Ql noqtis-seal-1
seal.
.It Bq Er NQEVRFY
The reply does not check: not granted, not a token in the form noqtis
reads, an imprint or nonce that differs, a signature or certificate that
does not verify, or no path to an anchor.
.It Bq Er NQELIM
More than 32 anchors, or a seal with the token over 1 MiB.
.It Bq Er NQEIO
.Pa noqtis.sig
cannot be read or written.
.It Bq Er NQEMEM
The allocation hook returned
.Dv NULL .
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
uint8_t nonce[8], req[128];
size_t qn;
const char *why;
int64_t gt;
nqrand(nonce, sizeof nonce);
nqtsreq("results", nonce, sizeof nonce, req, sizeof req, &qn);
/* POST req to the TSA; rsp, rn: the body of its reply */
if (nqtsput("results", rsp, rn, nonce, sizeof nonce, NULL, NULL, 0,
            &gt, &why) != NQOK)
  fprintf(stderr, "refused: %s\en", why);
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-check 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-seal 1 ,
.Xr nqchkt 3 ,
.Xr nqseal 3 ,
.Xr noqtis-capsule 5
.Sh STANDARDS
.Rs
.%R RFC 3161
.%T Internet X.509 Public Key Infrastructure Time-Stamp Protocol (TSP)
.%D August 2001
.Re
.Rs
.%R RFC 5816
.%T ESSCertIDv2 Update for RFC 3161
.%D April 2010
.Re
